# Illusionary Presence {1}{U}{U}: with three Moxen but one blue source it can't be cast; off Island, Mox Sapphire and Mox
# Ruby the pool is empty after. Both its upkeep triggers trigger at Bot1's turn 3 upkeep, the land type one put on the stack
# last. Bot1 chooses Tower, a land type that is no basic one (its 2005-11-01 ruling: any land subtype that exists): it gains
# towerwalk (CR 702.14c). Its cumulative upkeep {U} for one age counter can't be paid with Mox Ruby's {R} and is paid with the
# Island's {U}, the {R} left over (CR 702.24a). Bot2, whose only land is Urza's Tower, can't block it with Ornithopter. The
# landwalk lasts until end of turn (CR 514.2): gone in Bot2's upkeep, where no land type is asked ("your upkeep"). At turn 5
# the upkeep is {U}{U} for two counters; the choice offers land types only, not a creature type such as Elf (CR 205.3i), and
# Bot1 chooses Mine: minewalk, which neither Urza's Tower (an Urza's land, but no
# Mine) nor Bot2's Island lets walk, so Ornithopter blocks it and dies.

